Sure! To update a break node’s label to `'loopEnd'` only when it isn’t already set to that value, you can use the `updateBreak` function. Here’s how you’d call it:

```javascript
const result = await functions.updateBreak({
  node: /* your break node as a JSON string */,
  label: 'loopEnd'
});
```

Replace `/* your break node as a JSON string */` with the actual stringified representation of the break node you want to modify. The function will check the current label and replace it with `'loopEnd'` if needed.
